   {
    "@type": "FAQPage",
    "mainEntity": [
     {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How many days do I need to stay in Bangalore before I can safely fly back home?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
       "@type": "Answer",
       "text": "Most international patients should plan to stay in Bangalore for around 5 to 7 days. This usually allows enough time for arrival, in-person consultation, the procedure, initial healing, first review, and post-operative instructions. For larger sessions, repair cases, or patients travelling long distances, I may recommend a slightly longer stay. The final travel clearance depends on your healing and comfort after the procedure."
      }
     },
     {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can Neo Follicle Clinic assist me with hotel bookings, airport transfers, and my Medical Visa invitation letter?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
       "@type": "Answer",
       "text": "Yes, my team can guide international patients with travel-related coordination. We can assist with clinic-related documents such as a medical invitation letter where applicable. We can also guide you regarding nearby hotel areas, airport transfer options, and local stay planning. Many patients prefer staying in Marathahalli, Whitefield, Indiranagar, or Outer Ring Road because these areas are well-connected and suitable for international guests. Visa approval and travel permissions are handled by the relevant authorities, so patients should always check the latest official visa requirements before booking."
      }
     },
     {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How will Dr. Sandeep handle my post-operative follow-ups once I return to my home country?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
       "@type": "Answer",
       "text": "After you return home, we continue follow-up care digitally. You can share progress photos through WhatsApp, email, or other agreed communication channels. We may also schedule video reviews when needed. We usually monitor healing, scab shedding, redness, shedding phase, early growth, and long-term density improvement through scheduled photo updates. This allows us to stay connected with you throughout your recovery and growth journey."
      }
     },
     {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Are the clinic’s safety, hygiene, and graft-survival standards identical to clinics in the US or UK?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
       "@type": "Answer",
       "text": "At Neo Follicle, we follow strict sterilization protocols, medical-grade hygiene practices, careful graft handling, and internationally accepted hair transplant principles. Our goal is to maintain high standards of clinical safety, hygiene, and graft survival comparable to reputable clinics in developed countries. The lower cost in India is mainly because of lower operational expenses, not because of lower standards of care. However, patients should understand that outcomes depend on multiple factors, including donor quality, graft handling, surgical planning, post-op care, healing response, and long-term hair loss progression."
      }
     },
     {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Is there a language barrier for international patients?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
       "@type": "Answer",
       "text": "No. At Neo Follicle, the doctor and the medical team communicate fluently in English. We explain the consultation, procedure, medication schedule, aftercare instructions, and follow-up process clearly. International patients should feel comfortable asking questions at every stage."
      }
     },
     {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Is Bangalore safe and comfortable for international patients?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
       "@type": "Answer",
       "text": "Bangalore is one of India’s most international-friendly cities. It has a large global professional community, modern hospitals, international hotels, good transport options, and strong English-speaking support across healthcare and hospitality. Areas such as Marathahalli, Whitefield, Indiranagar, and Outer Ring Road are commonly used by international visitors and medical travelers."
      }
     },
     {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can I travel alone for my hair transplant?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
       "@type": "Answer",
       "text": "Many patients do travel alone, especially for smaller or moderate hair transplant sessions. However, if you are undergoing a large session, travelling from a very long distance, or feeling anxious, it may be helpful to bring a family member or friend. My team will guide you based on your procedure plan and comfort level."
      }
     },
     {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "When will I see the final results after returning home?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
       "@type": "Answer",
       "text": "Hair transplant results take time. Most patients begin to see early growth around 3 to 4 months. Visible improvement is usually seen around 6 months. Good density develops between 9 and 12 months. Final maturation may take 12 to 18 months, especially in the crown area. We guide international patients through this entire timeline using digital follow-up."
      }
     }
